  "details": "I am using contact senders and receivers for driving 2D “eye tracking” on a stylized model base. I have 4 senders and 4 receivers (2 for each eye) for getting the horizontal and vertical distance using VRChat’s built in eye-look stuff. These should always be active and getting proximity floats.\n\nI will launch the game and load into my home world with the avatar on. Everything will initialize properly as the proximity floats are updating as expected for the blend trees. The overlay shows the receivers as green.\n\nWhen I change worlds, 100% of the time it will refuse to initialize the receivers when I load into the same avatar in the new world. The overlay shows the receivers as blue/cyan and all the proximity floats are 0.00. I either have to reset the avatar or change out of and then back into the original avatar for the receivers to initialize.\n\nI have 3 separate versions of this avatar that all do the same issue.\n\nrelevant footage https://youtu.be/0zvQit0EtQI",
